<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rova of Antananarivo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rova of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antananarivo">Antananarivo</a> is the royal palace complex of the Merina kingdom on the highest hill of Antananarivo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. It held the palaces and tombs of the Merina rulers from the seventeenth century, including the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manjakamiadana">Manjakamiadana</a> palace, built of wood and later encased in stone. A fire in 1995 destroyed most of its buildings, and restoration has continued since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rova-of-antananarivo.jpg" alt="Rova of Antananarivo" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hery Zo Rakotondramanana · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reconstructed_Rova_Antananarivo_Madagascar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
